{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source && sed -n 1487,1493p raft.go; cd ../draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Source-derived narrowing of the point just named as open on the empty-configuration question, using code already read for this account: appendEntries records whatever sender arrives as the node's leader, with no membership test on that sender, and the follower loop only clears a known leader when heartbeats stop. In a live cluster whose legitimate leader keeps heartbeating, the restarted node's leader field therefore converges back on that leader; the residual exposure is any window in which a different sender's AppendEntries arrives while the legitimate leader is quiet, plus the entry acceptance already measured. This is reasoning from the cited source, not a measurement, and it is recorded as such.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"7e10640e7212486b94a80f04b69febc2-question-1\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"9d28f043326440548185371b0d4f375a-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-runfollower\\\",\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\",\\\"s-commit-tracking-contract\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"7e6d5b3d49464a84ba43f7f9305ea5b6\\\":[19,20,21],\\\"e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1\\\":[19,20],\\\"f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75\\\":[6,7],\\\"e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75e2\\\":[6,7]},\n   \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Four receipts of the same harness file answer this question from one recovery state (an empty configuration after a RestoreCommittedLogs restart): two runs state the vote and pre-vote admission (f418b9d6ab8841faa9ab6c35ce1fcd75 and e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9 at indices 6 and 7), one states the leadership acceptance and the election-gating control (e87ee87274544b3ba836dffb93a7ecb1 at indices 19 and 20), and one states the entry path as well (7e6d5b3d49464a84ba43f7f9305ea5b6 at indices 19, 20 and 21).\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: an empty recovered configuration removes participation checks on every path the question covers, while the node's own participation is gated off. Votes, leadership, entries and the gate control are measured as recorded above. Where a live cluster is concerned, the source bounds the effect in a way the single-node probes could not: appendEntries records whatever sender arrives as the node's leader without any membership test, and the follower loop clears a known leader only when contact stops, so a restarted node sharing a cluster with a legitimate leader that keeps heartbeating converges back on that leader; the residual exposure is a window in which another sender's AppendEntries arrives while the legitimate leader is quiet, together with the entry acceptance measured here. That statement is source-derived from the cited appendEntries and follower-loop ranges, not measured in a multi-node probe.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The empty-list leniency in the vote handlers is intentional for cluster bootstrap, and appendEntries has always trusted the sender's identity; what makes both harmful here is that the node's own recovery produces an empty configuration in a cluster that is not being bootstrapped.\\\",\n    \\\"The probe supplied the sender's identity and term rather than producing them through an election, so the requests are legal messages rather than a real campaign; a sender with a stale term is still rejected.\\\",\n    \\\"The node's own election gating is intact, so the failure is asymmetric: it admits others while suppressing itself, which also means it cannot repair the configuration by winning an election.\\\",\n    \\\"Source-derived bound for a live cluster: because the legitimate leader keeps heartbeating the node, the node's recorded leader converges back on it, so a durable split of the node's leader view needs the legitimate leader to be quiet while another sender's AppendEntries arrives; this is argued from the cited source ranges rather than from a multi-node measurement.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Measured on in-memory single-node clusters with the repository's in-memory transport and commit-tracking store; production transports, authentication and network behaviour are not covered.\\\",\n    \\\"The entry phase used one command entry with no configuration semantics, so the FSM effect recorded is a single applied command.\\\",\n    \\\"The probe does not measure how long the empty configuration persists in a cluster without membership traffic; that follows from the repair path rather than from a timed observation.\\\",\n    \\\"The multi-node behaviour described above is source-derived: no measurement covers a restarted node that shares a cluster with a legitimate leader, so the convergence and the residual window are unmeasured.\\\"\n   ]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/update.json'\nu=json.load(open(p))\nu['interpretations'][0]['executions']['e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9']=[6,7]\nu['interpretations'][0]['executions'].pop('e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75e2',None)\njson.dump(u,open(p,'w'),indent=2); print('fixed receipt id')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
